{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "ישראל ותחת רגליו", :translit "yisrael u-tachat raglav", :gloss "Israel, and under His feet"} {:he "ודמות פניהם פני אדם", :translit "u-dmut pneihem pnei adam", :gloss "and the likeness of their faces was the face of a man"} {:he "תמים", :translit "tamim", :gloss "complete/perfect"} {:he "יעקב התחת אלהים אני", :translit "ya'akov ha-tachat elohim anokhi", :gloss "Jacob, am I in place of Elohim?"} {:he "אנכי", :translit "anokhi", :gloss "I"} {:he "כסא", :translit "kisse", :gloss "throne"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "אנכי", :b "כסא"} {:kind :other, :note "Reads the word תמים in the sefer Torah; this is a variant matter."}], :frame {:text "Rav said that underneath the throne of glory was a likeness like the image of Jacob, as stated at Pesikta Rabbati 46 and Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 4. The four creatures seen by Ezekiel each bore a face; the face of the ox was replaced by the face of an angel to avoid recalling Israel's sin of the golden calf, per Chullin 91a. Jacob's challenge to his sons, \"Am I in place of Elohim?\" (Genesis 30:2), is linked here to the divine throne by gematria.", :sources ["Genesis 30:2" "Pirkei de-Rabbi Eliezer 4" "Pesikta Rabbati 46" "Chullin 91a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לבנת", :translit "livnat", :gloss "brick / brickwork"} {:he "ובשיחור לבנת", :translit "u-vi-shichor livnat", :gloss "and at Shihor-libnath"} {:he "והיא שם עיר", :translit "ve-hi shem ir", :gloss "and it is the name of a city"} {:he "שעבורן של ישראל", :translit "she-avuran shel yisrael", :gloss "the servitude of Israel"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["לבנת" "לבנת"]} {:kind :other, :note "Other occurrence is in Joshua, where it is a city name."}], :frame {:text "The word לבנת in Exodus 24:10 is read as \"brickwork.\" God showed the elders something resembling a brick so Israel would remember the brick-making of their bondage, per Chullin 91a. The other occurrence of לבנת is the place-name Shihor-libna